  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Which of the following is congruent to $0$ modulo $14?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, recall that \n\n$$\na≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a=kn,\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in Z.$ In other words, when $a$ is divided by $n,$ there is no remainder. This means that any integer multiple of $14$ is congruent to $0$ modulo $14.$\n\nTherefore, since $14\\,|\\,(-84),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n-84≡(-6)\\cdot 14≡(-6)\\cdot 0≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14).\n$$\n\nNone of the other options are multiples of $14.$",
